        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): reject zero-value cron.sessionRetention to prevent silent data loss",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nConfiguring `cron.sessionRetention: \"0h\"` (or `\"0d\"`, `\"0ms\"`) is silently accepted by Zod config validation. `parseDurationMs(\"0h\")` returns `0` without throwing, so the `superRefine` passes the value. Unlike `heartbeat.every` — where `\"0m\"` is the documented disable sentinel with a runtime `ms <= 0` guard in `resolveHeartbeatIntervalMs` — `cron.sessionRetention` uses `false` (boolean) to disable and `resolveRetentionMs` returns `0ms` directly with no guard. `sweepCronRunSessions` then computes `cutoff = now - 0 = now`, matching all cron run sessions for immediate deletion.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe `superRefine` only checks whether `parseDurationMs` throws — treating any non-throwing return value (including `0`) as valid. `parseDurationMs` itself returns `0` for zero inputs (not an error), and `resolveRetentionMs` does not defend against it. The positivity gate belongs in schema validation where config-level diagnostics surface the misconfiguration before runtime damage.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAn operator who accidentally sets `cron.sessionRetention: \"0h\"` (e.g. mistyping `\"24h\"`) will see all cron run sessions immediately deleted on the next sweep cycle with no error. After this fix, the misconfiguration is caught at config load time with a clear diagnostic. The documented disable path (`false`) is unaffected.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Claim proved**: `cron.sessionRetention` rejects zero intervals (non-documented paths) while accepting positive intervals and `false` (documented disable).\n- **Current head**: `e78e3377739eb180fb7ca36372964e18ff4af3a8`.\n- **Commands / artifacts**:\n  - `node --import tsx` runtime bug proof (before fix)\n  - `pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json` (after fix)\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/schema.test.ts`\n  - `git diff --check`\n\n### Runtime bug proof (before fix — `resolveRetentionMs` returns 0ms)\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx -e \"\nimport { resolveRetentionMs } from './src/cron/session-reaper.ts';\nconsole.log(resolveRetentionMs({sessionRetention: '0h'}));\n\"\n0\n```\n\n`0ms` → `cutoff = now - 0 = now` → all cron run sessions immediately deleted.\n\n### After fix: zero values rejected by config validation\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/cfg.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json\n{\n  \"valid\": false,\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"cron.sessionRetention\",\n      \"message\": \"duration must be positive (use ms, s, m, h, d), e.g. 24h\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### After fix: positive intervals still accepted\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/cfg.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json\n{\"valid\":true,\"path\":\"/tmp/cfg.json5\",\"warnings\":[]}\n```\n\n### After fix: `false` (documented disable) unaffected\n\nConfig `cron: { sessionRetention: false }` continues to disable pruning as documented in `docs/cli/cron.md`.\n\n### Focused Vitest\n\n1 test file, 59 tests passed (3 new + 56 existing unaffected).\n\n### Diff whitespace checks\n\n`git diff --check` passed.\n\n- **Not tested / proof gaps**: None.",
